 {"id": "AUG-072", "title": "[P2] start's seed remember fails 400 VALIDATION_ERROR on every fresh run ('Missing required fields: key, domain, content') — the seed note never stores", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 1, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-24 22:13:31", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "reasoning": "Found live 2026-09-24 foreman tick auger-2026-09-24-22-04-29 while staging the AUG-062 repro: fresh ns init+start prints \"remember /auger/<pid>/seed failed (400): {'error': 'Missing required fields: key, domain, content', 'code': 'VALIDATION_ERROR'}\" and continues; the seed note is silently never stored. Reproduced twice (ns auger-probe-1790287737, auger-probe-1790287833). The remember payload omits fields DuckBrain's declared-table validation requires. Fix direction: send the required key/domain/content fields in the seed remember payload (or drop the remember deliberately — but a silent 400 on a fresh install is a bad first-run signal either way). start otherwise completes: project row created, namespace usable.", "completed_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "Closed by dogfood run 8 (2026-09-25 failure-semantics leg): a fresh start (ns auger-df8-failure on a scratch substrate :3121) stored its seed with NO remember-400, live-verifying commit e3df3af ('fix: AUG-072 fresh-start seed remember no longer 400s on empty seed', HEAD at tick start). The row was left pending when the fix landed — bookkeeping drift, not a code gap. Note: the fix commit itself is at HEAD e3df3af with CI green; this close adds only the verification evidence (docs/dogfood/2026-09-25-failure-semantics-integration.md)."}
 {"id": "AUG-073", "title": "[P2] CONTRIBUTING's contributor verification loop is wrong on 3 axes: points at substrate-bound smoke.sh instead of the substrate-free gate.sh, declares 8 of 13 verbs as 'the API', and no machine-readable version exists anywhere", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 02:16:38", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 02:16:38", "reasoning": "PM lane sweep 2026-09-25 (premises verified live, not hunter claims): (1) CONTRIBUTING.md 'Run the smoke test' is the ONLY pre-PR check it names, and tests/smoke.sh hard-requires a live DuckBrain+JEV substrate; tests/gate.sh — the script CI actually runs on every push/PR (ci.yml comment lines 3-12, AUGER_CI guard) — is never mentioned, so a substrate-less contributor has no documented pre-PR check. (2) CONTRIBUTING 'The verbs are the API' lists init,start,ask,answer,check,status,toggle,dump but the real top-level surface is 13 verbs (auger --help): bundle, propagate, feedback, recall, verdict are uncovered by the breaking-change contract. (3) No __version__ in auger.py, no --version flag, no CHANGELOG.md, no pyproject.toml: 'v0.1' exists only as README prose, bug reports have no version to quote, future tags have no in-code anchor. Related but distinct from RELEASE-001 (tags/releases exist nowhere) and AUG-039 (README token claim) — this row is the contributor-docs + version-string axis. Pass criteria: CONTRIBUTING names tests/gate.sh as the substrate-free pre-PR check (CI runs it with live arms skipped); the API-stability contract covers all 13 verbs matching --help, with a rule that adding a verb updates the list; python3 auger.py --version (or AUGER_VERSION) prints a version whose single source lives in auger.py; CHANGELOG.md exists with a v0.1 entry.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c43de1ace435dc34d7fac2983ced21ff81ed731f5481857b15af8455af120ee2"}}
 {"id": "AUG-074", "title": "[P1] init hardcodes ~/duckbrain/namespaces for declaration files and exits 0 on a 0/14 tally — a non-default substrate namespaces path yields a green init that breaks at start", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 8 (failure-semantics leg). ns_dir() (auger.py:318) is os.path.expanduser('~/duckbrain/namespaces/<ns>') — hardcoded, while the substrate honors DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH (run 8 used a scratch substrate on :3121 with namespaces under /tmp). Live result: init wrote the 14 declaration files into the PRODUCTION tree on the control host and printed 'declared: 0/14 tables' plus a WARNING listing all 14 as 'not visible to the API yet' — then exited 0; start then died with \"insert project failed (404): Table 'project' not found\". VERBS.md's init contract says the declared tally is how the count is checked, but a 0/14 tally still exits 0. A user following the README's own DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR fresh-install advice plus a non-default namespaces path gets a broken install with a green-looking init. Fix direction: (a) resolve the declaration directory from the substrate's configured namespaces path (registry entry from GET /api/namespaces or an env passthrough), not from ~; (b) exit non-zero (or refuse) when the tally is 0/14 on a create/init run. Minor same-family friction: 'start -p <id>' silently ignores -p (minted P-20260925103605 despite the flag); an ignored-flag hint would save a round-trip."}
-{"id": "AUG-075", "title": "[P1] check and recall FAIL OPEN on a dead substrate: rc=0 'no stored evidence matched — treat as a new question' / empty recall while the store is unreachable", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 8: killed the substrate (kill -9) and probed every verb. status/dump/ask/answer/feedback/verdict all fail CLOSED — rc=1, \"transport: Connection refused\", <1s, nothing hangs, nothing invented. But check returned rc=0 with 'no stored evidence matched — treat as a new question' while D-001 (a decision closing exactly that question, verified intact after restart) sat in the unreachable store, and recall returned rc=0 with an empty result set. VERBS.md's honesty contract ('a refused write exits non-zero and says why'; check 'never writes anything', and drifted records must not be silently misreported) is upheld for writes and broken for the two retrieval verbs: 'we hold nothing' is reported when the truth is 'we cannot reach what we hold'. A user trusts the false negative and re-drills an answered decision. Fix direction: distinguish empty-answer-set (200, 0 rows) from transport failure in the db_select/db_retrieve callers of check and recall, and fail closed (rc=1, 'substrate unreachable') exactly as write verbs already do — two call sites."}
+{"id": "AUG-075", "title": "[P1] check and recall FAIL OPEN on a dead substrate: rc=0 'no stored evidence matched \u2014 treat as a new question' / empty recall while the store is unreachable", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T19:45:00Z", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 8: killed the substrate (kill -9) and probed every verb. status/dump/ask/answer/feedback/verdict all fail CLOSED \u2014 rc=1, \"transport: Connection refused\", <1s, nothing hangs, nothing invented. But check returned rc=0 with 'no stored evidence matched \u2014 treat as a new question' while D-001 (a decision closing exactly that question, verified intact after restart) sat in the unreachable store, and recall returned rc=0 with an empty result set. VERBS.md's honesty contract ('a refused write exits non-zero and says why'; check 'never writes anything', and drifted records must not be silently misreported) is upheld for writes and broken for the two retrieval verbs: 'we hold nothing' is reported when the truth is 'we cannot reach what we hold'. A user trusts the false negative and re-drills an answered decision. Fix direction: distinguish empty-answer-set (200, 0 rows) from transport failure in the db_select/db_retrieve callers of check and recall, and fail closed (rc=1, 'substrate unreachable') exactly as write verbs already do \u2014 two call sites. PM 09-25: fix landed in 715be71 (09-25 08:03, SubstrateError fail-closed across check/recall/ask/gate_question + docs/VERBS.md). Evidence: pytest 3 fail-closed cases (test_recall_transport_failure_is_a_failure_not_an_empty_store, test_check_fails_closed_when_the_substrate_is_dead, test_gate_question_reports_a_dead_substrate_as_an_error) = 3 passed 0.03s. Closed by PM lane, verified live.", "commit_hash": "715be71"}
 {"id": "AUG-076", "title": "[P1] answer is not crash-atomic: killing the substrate inside the write window commits the decision+option table rows, fails the memory remember, and the natural retry duplicates the choice instead of repairing", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 10:55:00", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 8: staged kills at +50/+150/+210ms of a ~235ms answer; the +210ms kill landed inside the memory remember. Result: rc=1 honest failure ('remember .../D-002 failed (0): transport: Remote end closed connection without response'), but after restart status showed decisions 2 | options 5 — the decision and option table rows COMMITTED while the memory write failed. recall cannot see D-002 (only seed + D-001 return), so the decision is invisible to every retrieval surface forever. The user's natural recovery — rerun the same answer — mints D-003 (AUG-069's highest-id mint working as designed) and the domain now carries two ACTIVE decisions recording the same choice: no supersession, no warning (AUG-070's dump duplicate-id warning only fires for duplicate ids; D-002/D-003 are distinct), no memory entry for the earlier one. Crash-consistency sibling of AUG-070 (concurrent writers). Fix direction (any one changes the failure mode): (a) write the decision as status=provisional and flip to decided only after the remember succeeds; (b) a consistency self-check on status/dump flagging decisions with no memory entry (query the store by key prefix); (c) answer's retry path detects an identical unembedded decision and repairs instead of minting."}
 {"id": "AUG-077", "title": "[P1] current-mode dump renders a self-contradictory configuration silently: the contradiction detector exists only in hypothetical mode", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 17:45:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 17:45:00", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 9 (mind-change surface, ns df9 on scratch substrate :3122). After toggle --on D-001-O2 (toggle itself is honest: it deactivates sibling D-001-O1 and prints '[siblings off - one option per decision D-001: D-001-O1 (1)]'), dump in current mode renders chosen-label (O1, the answer's --chosen) AND active-checkbox (O2, the toggle) with no warning - the exact two-valued configuration AUG-070 fixed for duplicate-id collisions, now reachable through the legitimate mind-change path. The contradiction detector ALREADY EXISTS: dump --config D-001=<other option> prints a 'CONTRADICTIONS WITH THE RECORD' block quoting the recorded why-not - but that pass runs only for the hypothetical path. A user who changes their mind via toggle and dumps gets a contradictory 'current spec' presented as truth with zero signal. Reproduced: dump | grep -ci CONTRADICT == 0 on the broken current state, == 1 for the same state as a hypothesis. Fix direction: run the same contradiction pass in current mode (chosen option row vs active option row of the same decision) and print the same CONTRADICTIONS block; AUG-070's duplicate-id warning fires only on identical ids, D-001's chosen/active mismatch has distinct ids so it needs its own check in the current path."}
 {"id": "AUG-078", "title": "[P1] recall ranks the superseded decision EQUAL (0.992) with its successor, unmarked: retrieval tells the old story with equal authority", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25 17:45:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25 17:45:00", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 9. After answer --supersedes D-001 (D-002 recorded, edge E-000003 created, D-001 status moved to superseded, facets refreshed - the supersede mechanism itself works and printed all of it), recall 'which option did we choose for question meaning' returns D-002 at 0.992 AND D-001 at 0.992, both snippets reading 'Decision D-00X: we chose <X>' with no superseded marker. A user reading the top hits gets two contradictory answers with identical scores and no way to tell which one is live. AUG-030 closed the configuration axis (dump active state); this is the retrieval axis the same fix never touched. The edge table already carries the supersedes relation and answer prints 'status -> superseded', so the data needed to rank or annotate is present at recall time. Fix direction: either rank superseded rows below their successor (deterministic when a successor exists) or annotate the snippet '[superseded by D-002]' in recall output; check is unaffected (its 1.000 hit was D-001's memory row and still correctly gated the re-ask), this is a recall/dump-of-results presentation and ranking fix."}
